ble.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4426" data-end=3D"4429">
<h1 data-start=3D"4431" data-end=3D"4467">=F0=9F=94=9F The Real Answer in O=
ne Sentence</h1>
<p data-start=3D"4469" data-end=3D"4502">Hibernate hydrates first because:<=
/p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"4504" data-end=3D"4599">
<p data-start=3D"4506" data-end=3D"4599">The ResultSet is a transport mecha=
nism for identifiers, not a trusted canonical entity state.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"4601" data-end=3D"4633">L2 cache stores canonical state.</=
p>
<p data-start=3D"4635" data-end=3D"4676">ResultSet stores query-specific ro=
w data.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4678" data-end=3D"4708">They serve different purposes.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4710" data-end=3D"4713">
<h1 data-start=3D"4715" data-end=3D"4751">1=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A31=EF=B8=8F=E2=
=83=A3 Deeper Architectural Reason</h1>
<p data-start=3D"4753" data-end=3D"4786">Hibernate architecture separates:<=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"4788" data-end=3D"4881">
<li data-start=3D"4788" data-end=3D"4805">
<p data-start=3D"4790" data-end=3D"4805">Query execution</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4806" data-end=3D"4831">
<p data-start=3D"4808" data-end=3D"4831">Entity state management</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4832" data-end=3D"4850">
<p data-start=3D"4834" data-end=3D"4850">Cache management</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4851" data-end=3D"4881">
<p data-start=3D"4853" data-end=3D"4881">Persistence context identity</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4883" data-end=3D"4935">If Hibernate used ResultSet direct=
ly as final state:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4937" data-end=3D"5099">
<li data-start=3D"4937" data-end=3D"4966">
<p data-start=3D"4939" data-end=3D"4966">L2 would become meaningless</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4967" data-end=3D"5005">
<p data-start=3D"4969" data-end=3D"5005">Dirty checking would be inconsiste=
nt</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5006" data-end=3D"5060">
<p data-start=3D"5008" data-end=3D"5060">Repeatable read semantics inside S=
ession would break</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5061" data-end=3D"5099">
