<h1 data-start=3D"129" data-end=3D"155">1=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 What Is a Data =
Grid?</h1>
<p data-start=3D"157" data-end=3D"222">A <strong data-start=3D"159" data-en=
d=3D"172">data grid</strong> (specifically an <em data-start=3D"190" data-e=
nd=3D"211">in-memory data grid</em>, IMDG) is:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"224" data-end=3D"350">
<p data-start=3D"226" data-end=3D"350">A distributed, in-memory, horizontal=
ly scalable data store that can execute queries and computations over the d=
ata it holds.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"352" data-end=3D"385">It is not just a key-value cache.</p=
>
<p data-start=3D"387" data-end=3D"409">It typically provides:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"411" data-end=3D"606">
<li data-start=3D"411" data-end=3D"459">
<p data-start=3D"413" data-end=3D"459">Distributed storage (partitioned acr=
oss nodes)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"460" data-end=3D"473">
<p data-start=3D"462" data-end=3D"473">Replication</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"474" data-end=3D"496">
<p data-start=3D"476" data-end=3D"496">Distributed querying</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"497" data-end=3D"507">
<p data-start=3D"499" data-end=3D"507">Indexing</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"508" data-end=3D"535">
<p data-start=3D"510" data-end=3D"535">Compute execution on data</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"536" data-end=3D"568">
<p data-start=3D"538" data-end=3D"568">Optional transactional support</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"569" data-end=3D"606">
<p data-start=3D"571" data-end=3D"606">Near real-time consistency controls<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"608" data-end=3D"617">Examples:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"619" data-end=3D"744">
<li data-start=3D"619" data-end=3D"660">
