<hr data-start=3D"3556" data-end=3D"3559">
<h1 data-start=3D"3561" data-end=3D"3605">6=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 What L2 Cache=
 Guarantees (and Doesn=E2=80=99t)</h1>
<p data-start=3D"3607" data-end=3D"3623">With READ_WRITE:</p>
<p data-start=3D"3625" data-end=3D"3786">=E2=9C=85 No dirty reads from cach=
e<br data-start=3D"3652" data-end=3D"3655">
=E2=9C=85 No stale entry after successful commit<br data-start=3D"3695" dat=
a-end=3D"3698">
=E2=9C=85 Version-based protection<br data-start=3D"3724" data-end=3D"3727"=
>
=E2=9D=8C No serializable isolation<br data-start=3D"3754" data-end=3D"3757=
">
=E2=9D=8C No cross-entity atomicity</p>
<p data-start=3D"3788" data-end=3D"3850">L2 cache consistency is per-entity=
, not per-transaction graph.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3852" data-end=3D"3855">
<h1 data-start=3D"3857" data-end=3D"3882">7=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 What About Qu=
eries?</h1>
<p data-start=3D"3884" data-end=3D"3894">Important:</p>
<p data-start=3D"3896" data-end=3D"3942">Query cache is much harder to keep=
 consistent.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3944" data-end=3D"3970">If you enable query cache:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3972" data-end=3D"4090">
<li data-start=3D"3972" data-end=3D"4027">
<p data-start=3D"3974" data-end=3D"4027">Any update to table invalidates re=
lated query regions</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4028" data-end=3D"4074">
<p data-start=3D"4030" data-end=3D"4074">High write frequency =E2=86=92 con=
stant invalidation</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4075" data-end=3D"4090">
<p data-start=3D"4077" data-end=3D"4090">Low hit ratio</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4092" data-end=3D"4115">In write-heavy systems:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"4117" data-end=3D"4137">
<p data-start=3D"4119" data-end=3D"4137">Avoid query cache.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"4139" data-end=3D"4208">Entity cache is fine.<br>
Query cache is fragile under concurrent writes.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4210" data-end=3D"4213">
<h1 data-start=3D"4215" data-end=3D"4257">8=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Common Mistak=
es That Cause Staleness</h1>
<p data-start=3D"4259" data-end=3D"4468">=E2=9D=8C No <code data-start=3D"4=
264" data-end=3D"4274">@Version</code><br data-start=3D"4274" data-end=3D"4=
277">
=E2=9D=8C Using NONSTRICT_READ_WRITE on mutable data<br data-start=3D"4321"=
 data-end=3D"4324">
=E2=9D=8C Running multiple app nodes with local cache<br data-start=3D"4369=
" data-end=3D"4372">
=E2=9D=8C Using query cache on frequently updated tables<br data-start=3D"4=
420" data-end=3D"4423">
=E2=9D=8C Mixing direct JDBC updates with Hibernate</p>
