<p data-start=3D"2308" data-end=3D"2312">DTO:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2313" data-end=3D"2381">
<li data-start=3D"2313" data-end=3D"2324">
<p data-start=3D"2315" data-end=3D"2324">Immutable</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2325" data-end=3D"2351">
<p data-start=3D"2327" data-end=3D"2351">Not managed by Hibernate</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2352" data-end=3D"2381">
<p data-start=3D"2354" data-end=3D"2381">Safe to cache independently</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2383" data-end=3D"2395">This avoids:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2396" data-end=3D"2460">
<li data-start=3D"2396" data-end=3D"2414">
<p data-start=3D"2398" data-end=3D"2414">Entity staleness</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2415" data-end=3D"2434">
<p data-start=3D"2417" data-end=3D"2434">Version conflicts</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2435" data-end=3D"2460">
<p data-start=3D"2437" data-end=3D"2460">Session identity issues</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2462" data-end=3D"2465">
<h1 data-start=3D"2467" data-end=3D"2496">5=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Architectural=
 Guideline</h1>
<p data-start=3D"2498" data-end=3D"2510">Never cache:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"2512" data-end=3D"2566">
<p data-start=3D"2514" data-end=3D"2566">Managed entities at service layer =
with Spring cache.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"2568" data-end=3D"2592">If you use Spring cache:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2594" data-end=3D"2690">
<li data-start=3D"2594" data-end=3D"2606">
<p data-start=3D"2596" data-end=3D"2606">Cache DTOs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2607" data-end=3D"2630">
<p data-start=3D"2609" data-end=3D"2630">Cache computed values</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2631" data-end=3D"2659">
<p data-start=3D"2633" data-end=3D"2659">Cache external API results</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2660" data-end=3D"2690">
<p data-start=3D"2662" data-end=3D"2690">Cache expensive aggregations</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2692" data-end=3D"2739">Let Hibernate manage entity cachin=
g internally.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2741" data-end=3D"2744">
<h1 data-start=3D"2746" data-end=3D"2775">6=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Performance P=
erspective</h1>
<p data-start=3D"2777" data-end=3D"2801">If L2 hit ratio is good:</p>
<p data-start=3D"2803" data-end=3D"2860">Spring cache around repository cal=
ls adds almost nothing.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2862" data-end=3D"2870">Because:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2872" data-end=3D"2960">
<li data-start=3D"2872" data-end=3D"2899">
<p data-start=3D"2874" data-end=3D"2899">L2 lookup is already O(1)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2900" data-end=3D"2939">
<p data-start=3D"2902" data-end=3D"2939">Object materialization still requi=
red</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2940" data-end=3D"2960">
<p data-start=3D"2942" data-end=3D"2960">No DB call already</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2962" data-end=3D"2987">You don=E2=80=99t gain much more.<=
/p>
<hr data-start=3D"2989" data-end=3D"2992">
<h1 data-start=3D"2994" data-end=3D"3019">7=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Multi-Node Sc=
enario</h1>
<p data-start=3D"3021" data-end=3D"3052">If you have multiple app nodes:</p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"3054" data-end=3D"3128">
<li data-start=3D"3054" data-end=3D"3088">
<p data-start=3D"3056" data-end=3D"3088">Hibernate L2 must be distributed</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3089" data-end=3D"3128">
<p data-start=3D"3091" data-end=3D"3128">Spring cache must also be distribu=
ted</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3130" data-end=3D"3191">Now you=E2=80=99ve doubled your di=
stributed consistency surface area.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3193" data-end=3D"3230">That=E2=80=99s complexity without =
clear gain.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3232" data-end=3D"3235">
<h1 data-start=3D"3237" data-end=3D"3272">8=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Clean Strateg=
y Recommendation</h1>
<p data-start=3D"3274" data-end=3D"3301">In most enterprise systems:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3303" data-end=3D"3341">Option A (simpler, usually enough=
)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3342" data-end=3D"3411">
<li data-start=3D"3342" data-end=3D"3380">
<p data-start=3D"3344" data-end=3D"3380">Hibernate L2 (READ_WRITE + @Versio=
n)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3381" data-end=3D"3411">
<p data-start=3D"3383" data-end=3D"3411">No Spring cache for entities</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3413" data-end=3D"3456">Option B (explicit application ca=
ching)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3457" data-end=3D"3518">
<li data-start=3D"3457" data-end=3D"3469">
<p data-start=3D"3459" data-end=3D"3469">Disable L2</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3470" data-end=3D"3518">
<p data-start=3D"3472" data-end=3D"3518">Use Spring cache for DTOs and spec=
ific queries</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3520" data-end=3D"3551">Option C (rarely justified)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3552" data-end=3D"3620">
<li data-start=3D"3552" data-end=3D"3579">
<p data-start=3D"3554" data-end=3D"3579">Hibernate L2 for entities</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3580" data-end=3D"3620">
<p data-start=3D"3582" data-end=3D"3620">Spring cache for DTO aggregations =
only</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3622" data-end=3D"3625">
<h1 data-start=3D"3627" data-end=3D"3651">9=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Decision Heur=
istic</h1>
<p data-start=3D"3653" data-end=3D"3657">Ask:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"3659" data-end=3D"3868">
<li data-start=3D"3659" data-end=3D"3709">
<p data-start=3D"3662" data-end=3D"3709">Are we caching identity lookups? =
=E2=86=92 Hibernate L2</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3710" data-end=3D"3768">
