<h1 data-start=3D"2115" data-end=3D"2145"><strong data-start=3D"2117" data-=
end=3D"2145">Key Performance Insights</strong></h1>
<ol data-start=3D"2147" data-end=3D"2846">
<li data-start=3D"2147" data-end=3D"2244">
<p data-start=3D"2150" data-end=3D"2244"><strong data-start=3D"2150" data-e=
nd=3D"2213">L2 cache helps only after hydration for repeated ID lookups</st=
rong>, not for dynamic predicates.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2245" data-end=3D"2358">
<p data-start=3D"2248" data-end=3D"2358"><strong data-start=3D"2248" data-e=
nd=3D"2276">Hydration is unavoidable</strong> because you need the entity I=
D to check L1/L2 and maintain identity guarantees.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2359" data-end=3D"2463">
<p data-start=3D"2362" data-end=3D"2463"><strong data-start=3D"2362" data-e=
nd=3D"2399">Dynamic queries always hit the DB</strong> =E2=80=94 joins, fil=
ters, and projections cannot be resolved from L2.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2464" data-end=3D"2563">
<p data-start=3D"2467" data-end=3D"2563"><strong data-start=3D"2467" data-e=
nd=3D"2486">DTO projections</strong> skip hydration and L2 entirely =E2=86=
=92 fastest for read-heavy, dynamic searches.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2564" data-end=3D"2650">
<p data-start=3D"2567" data-end=3D"2650"><strong data-start=3D"2567" data-e=
nd=3D"2595">Fetch joins / batch size</strong> help reduce N+1 issues when t=
raversing associations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2651" data-end=3D"2741">
<p data-start=3D"2654" data-end=3D"2741"><strong data-start=3D"2654" data-e=
nd=3D"2685">Read-only hints + streaming</strong> reduce memory and CPU over=
head for large result sets.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2742" data-end=3D"2846">
<p data-start=3D"2745" data-end=3D"2846"><strong data-start=3D"2745" data-e=
nd=3D"2767">Query plan caching</strong> reduces SQL compilation overhead fo=
r repeated dynamic Specification queries.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"2848" data-end=3D"2851">
<h1 data-start=3D"2853" data-end=3D"2867"><strong data-start=3D"2855" data-=
end=3D"2867">Takeaway</strong></h1>
<ul data-start=3D"2869" data-end=3D"3223">
<li data-start=3D"2869" data-end=3D"3020">
<p data-start=3D"2871" data-end=3D"3020"><strong data-start=3D"2871" data-e=
nd=3D"2896">For dynamic searches:</strong> optimize the query itself (SQL, =
joins, projections), manage associations efficiently, and use batch fetchin=
g / streaming.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3021" data-end=3D"3121">
<p data-start=3D"3023" data-end=3D"3121"><strong data-start=3D"3023" data-e=
nd=3D"3053">L2 cache is mostly helpful</strong> for repeated single-entity =
lookups or immutable reference tables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3122" data-end=3D"3223">
<p data-start=3D"3124" data-end=3D"3223"><strong data-start=3D"3124" data-e=
nd=3D"3152">Spring Cache can be used</strong> only for immutable DTOs or re=
ference data, not for managed entities.</p>
</li>
</ul>
