</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2324" data-end=3D"2327">
<h1 data-start=3D"2329" data-end=3D"2381"><strong data-start=3D"2331" data-=
end=3D"2381">5=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Where You Can Actually Improve Performance=
</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"2383" data-end=3D"2414">Instead of ordering predicates:</p=
>
<ol data-start=3D"2416" data-end=3D"3262">
<li data-start=3D"2416" data-end=3D"2600">
<p data-start=3D"2419" data-end=3D"2477"><strong data-start=3D"2419" data-e=
nd=3D"2443">Ensure indexes exist</strong> on frequently filtered columns.</=
p>
<ul data-start=3D"2481" data-end=3D"2600">
<li data-start=3D"2481" data-end=3D"2535">
<p data-start=3D"2483" data-end=3D"2535">Single-column indexes for high-sel=
ectivity filters</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2539" data-end=3D"2600">
<p data-start=3D"2541" data-end=3D"2600">Composite indexes if multiple filt=
ers are always combined</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2602" data-end=3D"2733">
<p data-start=3D"2605" data-end=3D"2639"><strong data-start=3D"2605" data-e=
nd=3D"2637">Avoid unnecessary predicates</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"2643" data-end=3D"2733">
<li data-start=3D"2643" data-end=3D"2675">
<p data-start=3D"2645" data-end=3D"2675">Skip null or default filters</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2679" data-end=3D"2733">
<p data-start=3D"2681" data-end=3D"2733">Don=E2=80=99t generate OR conditio=
ns when simple IN can do</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2735" data-end=3D"2850">
<p data-start=3D"2738" data-end=3D"2767"><strong data-start=3D"2738" data-e=
nd=3D"2765">Use database statistics</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"2771" data-end=3D"2850">
<li data-start=3D"2771" data-end=3D"2813">
<p data-start=3D"2773" data-end=3D"2813">Analyze table statistics for optim=
izer</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2817" data-end=3D"2850">
<p data-start=3D"2819" data-end=3D"2850">PostgreSQL: <code data-start=3D"28=
31" data-end=3D"2848">ANALYZE orders;</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2852" data-end=3D"3053">
<p data-start=3D"2855" data-end=3D"2878"><strong data-start=3D"2855" data-e=
nd=3D"2876">Profile the query</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"2882" data-end=3D"3053">
<li data-start=3D"2882" data-end=3D"2968">
<p data-start=3D"2884" data-end=3D"2968"><code data-start=3D"2884" data-end=
=3D"2901">EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> (Postgres) or execution plan (MySQL) to se=
e actual row filtering</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2972" data-end=3D"3053">
<p data-start=3D"2974" data-end=3D"3053">Focus on actual bottlenecks: joins=
, aggregates, functions, or missing indexes</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3055" data-end=3D"3262">
<p data-start=3D"3058" data-end=3D"3085"><strong data-start=3D"3058" data-e=
nd=3D"3083">Filter early in joins</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"3089" data-end=3D"3262">
<li data-start=3D"3089" data-end=3D"3178">
<p data-start=3D"3091" data-end=3D"3178">Apply filters on joined tables in =
<code data-start=3D"3125" data-end=3D"3129">ON</code> clause if possible to=
 reduce intermediate rows</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3182" data-end=3D"3262">
<p data-start=3D"3184" data-end=3D"3262">Example: <code data-start=3D"3193"=
 data-end=3D"3227">JOIN customer c ON c.active=3Dtrue</code> instead of <co=
de data-start=3D"3239" data-end=3D"3260">WHERE c.active=3Dtrue</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
